        "ellura_comparison_block_1": {
          "type": "point",
          "settings": {
            "point_number": "01",
            "text": "<p><strong>ellura’s</strong> difference lies in its 36 mg of soluble, bioactive A-type PACs — a clinically backed formula with superior absorption and the highest concentration of active PACs, the key component to help reduce the ability of certain bacteria from adhering to the urinary tract.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_comparison_block_2": {
          "type": "point",
          "settings": {
            "point_number": "02",
            "text": "<p>Many products claim to have PACs, but if sourced from insoluble cranberry pomace (seeds, stems, skin, pulp), they remain trapped in fibre and cannot be absorbed by the body.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_comparison_block_3": {
          "type": "point",
          "settings": {
            "point_number": "03",
            "text": "<p>Clinical research shows that only supplements with the highest levels of soluble PACs, like ellura, deliver powerful urinary tract defence.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
